<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="029" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Re-profile and re-index a document after a version save (per-version analysis key)</title>
    <phase>2 Save flow</phase>
    <gate>023 merged (version save writes a new SPE version of the existing sprk_document)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in the BFF background-job path (idempotency of document analysis + indexing) consumed by every document-save surface; tags include bff-api, ai and jobs.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-surface blast radius: the analysis idempotency key and the index-replace semantics are shared by Email, Attachment, Compose and Office saves. Getting the key wrong either double-processes every save or silently never refreshes.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>023</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, jobs, indexing, save-flow, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>After task 023, a version save writes new bytes to the SAME `sprk_document` (same document id). Finalization then queues the AI profile job with the idempotency key `analysis-{documentId}-documentprofile`, and the handler skips an already-processed key — so the new version is never re-profiled or re-indexed. The profile card and Find results go stale after the first re-save. Make analysis and indexing refresh for a genuinely new version while staying idempotent for retries of the same version and unchanged for every other save.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the BFF job contract (ADR-004 / ADR-036), Service Bus idempotency, the document profile pipeline and the RAG indexing pipeline. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>A version save whose content differs from the previous version triggers exactly one re-profile and one re-index of that `sprk_document`; replaying or retrying the same version triggers nothing extra; a first save and every Email/Attachment/Compose save behave exactly as today; the index holds chunks for the current version only (no duplicates, no orphans).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Source: `notes/023-save-path-trace.md` §13 (task 023's open items, 2026-09-11). `UploadFinalizationWorker` queues `AppOnlyDocumentAnalysis` with idempotency key `analysis-{documentId}-documentprofile`, and that handler skips an already-processed key. A version keeps the same document id. The note suggests a per-version key (for example the drive-item version or a content hash). Re-locate every symbol by name — do not trust line numbers.
      Task 023 already hashes content into the save's idempotency key for version saves only (decision 3 in its trace note) — reuse that hash if it reaches the finalization payload, rather than computing a second one.
      Owner decision 2026-09-12: this gap is owned by THIS project (not handed off).
      Also unverified from 023: whether the app-only finalization jobs can read a version written by the user (OBO). If a live check becomes possible, record it; do not block on it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/023-save-path-trace.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/patterns/ai/indexing-pipeline.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/architecture/DOCUMENT-PROFILE-AND-AI-EXECUTION-MODELS.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: only a version save (a Document save that targeted an existing `sprk_document`) may produce a new analysis/index key. First saves and every Email, Attachment and Compose path keep their current key and behaviour byte-for-byte.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: idempotency. A Service Bus redelivery or client retry of the SAME version must be skipped exactly as today. The per-version discriminator must be deterministic for identical content (content hash or SPE version id), never a timestamp or random value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="indexing-pipeline">Scope: re-indexing. Pass `documentId` on every index call. Re-indexing a document must REPLACE its chunks — confirm the pipeline's delete/replace semantics for an existing document before relying on it; duplicate or orphan chunks are a defect.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Scope: any AI capability reached from job code goes through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; do not inject `IOpenAiClient` / `IPlaybookService` into CRUD code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. No new service registration unless the existing job handlers cannot be extended; justify per CLAUDE.md §11 if one is added.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. Prove (a) a differing version triggers one re-profile + one re-index, (b) the same version replayed triggers none, (c) a first save and an Email save produce the same keys as master. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: BFF hygiene (root CLAUDE.md §10) — publish size against a FRESH master build (Compress-Archive), CVE check, placement statement in notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <owner-decisions date="2026-09-15">
    <decision name="index-replace">Option B from notes/029-version-ai-refresh.md: for a VERSION re-index only, upload the new chunks first, then delete that document's leftover chunks beyond the new chunk count, in the SAME index the path wrote to (the per-record index name, not the tenant default). One new `IRagService` method is allowed for this. The document must never be left without chunks. Every other re-index path keeps today's behaviour.</decision>
    <decision name="existing-data">Stale chunks already in dev are dev data: no backfill or cleanup job.</decision>
    <decision name="revert-case">Close it in this task: every genuinely new version refreshes, even when its content repeats an earlier version (B, then A, then B refreshes three times). Retries and Service Bus redeliveries of the SAME save still skip. A content hash alone cannot do this; prefer a discriminator that identifies the version the save wrote (for example the SPE version id or eTag the version write returned, or the save job's id), and prove both halves by test.</decision>
    <decision name="check-the-save-first">Before building, verify whether the SAVE itself has the same revert problem: the version-save idempotency key includes a content hash (023 D-3 / 039), so a third save whose content matches an earlier save inside the idempotency window may be answered from the cache and never written to SPE. If it is, STOP and report with evidence and options - that is a silent lost edit on the save spine and needs its own decision; do not change the save key inside this task.</decision>
  </owner-decisions>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load project CLAUDE.md, `notes/023-save-path-trace.md`, the indexing-pipeline pattern and the document-profile architecture doc. Declare FULL, opus @ high, DIRECTIONAL. Run `/conflict-check` (BFF hot path).</step>
    <step order="1">Trace finalization → profile job → index job for a version save and a first save; write the trace (keys, skip checks, index replace semantics) to `notes/029-version-ai-refresh.md` before changing code.</step>
    <step order="2">Carry a deterministic per-version discriminator from the version save into the finalization payload and into the analysis/index idempotency keys — for version saves only.</step>
    <step order="3">Ensure re-indexing replaces the document's previous chunks.</step>
    <step order="4">Add the tests in the ADR-038 constraint; run the BFF build, the affected job/AI/Office tests, ArchTests, and the full `Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests` once.</step>
    <step order="5">Publish size + CVE; record deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If changing the key for version saves would change the key, retry or skip behaviour of ANY other save path, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the indexing pipeline has no way to replace an existing document's chunks (re-indexing would duplicate or orphan them), STOP and escalate — do not add a bespoke delete path without a decision.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the profile handler's skip logic is shared with a job type outside document analysis, STOP before modifying it and escalate the blast radius.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The finalization → `AppOnlyDocumentAnalysis` path and the RAG indexing pipeline already exist; the defect is only the idempotency key being per-document rather than per-version for version saves (023 trace §13).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extend the existing key composition and payload; no new job type, handler or route.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>After the first re-save of a Word document, its AI profile (task 021's Profile section) and its Find/semantic-search chunks describe the OLD content forever — users see a stale summary and search misses the new text.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/029-version-ai-refresh.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a version save whose content differs from the prior version, when finalization runs, then exactly one re-profile and one re-index are queued for that `sprk_document`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given the same version replayed (Service Bus redelivery or client retry), then no additional profile or index job runs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a first save, or an Email/Attachment/Compose save, then the analysis and index keys are identical to master.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a re-index, then the index holds chunks for the current version only — no duplicates and no orphans — proven by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` green; affected tests, ArchTests and the full suite pass; publish size vs a fresh master build and the CVE result are recorded in notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Created 2026-09-12 by the main session from task 023's open item (owner: "New task in this project"). Related: task 021 (Profile section reads what this job writes), task 024 (client version save), task 033/034 (Find).
  </notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
